      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome in. What brings you to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S003",
      "patient_response": "Well, it's mostly because... people keep telling me I'm not listening. Like, my supervisor at the plant, or my wife. They'll be talking right at me, looking me in the eye, and... a minute later I realize I only caught maybe half of what they said. Then I have to ask them to repeat it, which really sets my wife off. She hates repeating herself. Actually, we got into a huge fight about it last weekend when we were supposed to go to her sister's house. Her sister lives out in Springfield, you know, past the old mall they tore down? They're building some new apartment complex there now, but honestly, the traffic on that road is just terrible since they started the construction. I don't even know why they approved that zoning. But yeah, anyway, I just... I miss things people say to me.",
