    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "{\"intent\": \"Determine whether the difficulty is due to physical hearing impairment or inattention\", \"question\": \"When you miss what people are saying, do you have trouble physically hearing the sounds, or",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, my hearing is fine. I hear the actual sounds perfectly. We actually have to get our hearing checked every single year at the plant because of the noise levels on the floor. They bring in this little white trailer, and you sit in this tiny soundproof booth with headphones, and you just press a button when you hear a beep. I always pass it no problem. \n\nThe real issue is the earplugs they make us wear—they're those cheap orange foam ones that expand in your ear? They itch so bad. I was telling my buddy Mike we should just buy our own custom ones. Mike goes to the shooting range a lot, so he has these really nice molded ones. He’s got this crazy collection of vintage rifles, actually. We were supposed to go to a gun show together last month but his truck broke down. It’s a Chevy, and I told him the transmission on those years was notoriously bad, but... wait, sorry, what were we talking about? \n\nOh, right. Yeah, I hear people just fine, it's just like my brain isn't recording the words.",
