    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Nowadays as an adult, do you still feel physically restless or have trouble sitting still?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, I do. It's... it's like this pressure building up inside my chest and my legs. If I have to sit still for too long, like in a meeting or something, I feel like I've just got to move or do something right that second, or I'm gonna crawl right out of my skin. \n\nIt's actually why I like working the floor at the plant, honestly. I get to walk the line, check the machines. We use these massive hydraulic presses, and the vibration they make when they stamp the metal is wild. You can feel it in your boots. I had to buy new steel-toes last month because the soles on my old ones completely wore out from all the walking. I got them at Red Wing—man, those guys really know how to fit a boot. The guy there, I think his name was Jerry, he was telling me about how he used to work construction out in Colorado before he moved back here. Colorado's supposed to be beautiful. My wife wants to go there for our anniversary, maybe rent a cabin in the mountains. She found this place online that has a hot tub out on the deck, which sounds great, but I don't know if I could just sit in a hot tub for hours like she does. \n\nBut yeah, sitting still is... it's just really hard for me. I always end up bouncing my leg or pacing if I have to be in one place too long.",
